            <ArticleTitle>[Efficacy of 3-year prophylaxis of coronary heart disease risk factors in an organized population].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>47-51</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An organized community numbering 1563 men aged 20 to 59 years engaged in scientific activity were entered into an experimental and prophylactic study. The intervention measures were exercised in a high risk group with dyslipoproteinemia, borderline hypertension and coronary heart disease (CHD), mainly at the expense of alterations in nutrition. The three-year prophylaxis resulted in a 7-percent decrease in blood plasma cholesterol and a 13-percent fall in triglycerides. The prevalence of arterial hypertension declined by 3 and the excess body weight by 3.7 percent, which led to a 33-percent decrease in CHD risk development calculated with the aid of the R. P. Prochorskas risk logistic function. Advantages of the individual strategy of CHD prevention are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
